# An error of one's own (ER1): "code" []S_IGNAL "message" stops with
# error[code]: message, reported at the call as any error is, and
# stands where any value may (its type is free, as []P_ANIC's is).
== SOURCE
u:c_heck := { n -> n < 0 ? "negative" []S_IGNAL "n must be 0 or more"; n }
p_rint! u:c_heck 3
u:c_heck -1
p_rint! "not reached"
== TYPE
u:c_heck : Num a => a -> a
Int
Int
Char
== ERROR
error[negative]: n must be 0 or more at 27..69
